look at the December six Georgia runoff between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:10.740
incumbent Democratic Senator Raphael Warnock&nbsp;
and challenging Republican candidate Herschel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:15.780
Walker. Now, we've already talked about how&nbsp;
Herschel Walker has no business being senator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.740
from Georgia. I'm going to give you yet another&nbsp;
example of that a little bit later on in the show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.820
But one of the interesting questions has been,&nbsp;
is Donald Trump going to show up to try to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:30.480
Herschel Walker? Barack Obama is showing up to&nbsp;
try to help Raphael Warnock now that we know and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.580
he will be campaigning with him. But Donald Trump&nbsp;
has is apparently so toxic at this point in time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.680
that Republicans are trying to keep him as far&nbsp;
away from Georgia and as far away from Herschel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:47.580
Walker as possible. New York Times Reports Trump&nbsp;
Plans Limited Role In Georgia Senate Runoff. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:52.500
former president, who held two big rallies before&nbsp;
the state's two runoff elections two years ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:59.820
both of which Democrats won, will steer clear of&nbsp;
Georgia before next week's Senate election. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:06.420
when you look at why, you very quickly understand&nbsp;
it. Michael Bender writes for The New York Times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:11.040
Donald Trump will not cross the Florida state&nbsp;
line to campaign with Herschel Walker during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:16.860
the final week of the Georgia Senate runoff&nbsp;
election. After both camps decided, the former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.600
president's appearance carried more political&nbsp;
risks than rewards. Campaign officials for the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.120
Republicans said Monday. Do we believe that Trump&nbsp;
was sitting there going, You know what, it's true.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:34.320
I've become such a ticking time bomb and a hothead&nbsp;
and liability that it's probably best that I not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:41.460
go. Probably not. It's probably the people around&nbsp;
Trump who got together with those running Walker's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:48.180
